# is (str0m's ICE agent): the agent checks its pairs as Chrome does, on a
# loop of Chrome's (src/pacing.rs): which pair a turn checks, how often,
# when one is weak and checked every 62.5 ms, and when one is given up
# (15 s after its first unanswered check). As published each pair has a
# timer of its own that backs off from 250 ms to 3 s, so a connected pair
# was checked every 3 s, one whose answers stopped 0.25 to 3 s apart, and
# a remote that never answers 9 times in 16 s (Chrome: 25 beside a working
